From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quake3: accept the demo's UI API version 3

The Quake III Arena 1.11 demo ships vm/ui.qvm built against the API 3 UI
header.  id only ever added UI traps at the end of the enum after that
release, so the API 3 UI runs fine against FTE's API 4/6 trap table - it
is the same table ioquake3 exposes to old mods.  FTE's UI_Start rejected
anything but 4 or 6, which killed the demo menu and left the client with
a spawned-but-empty listen server (no menu means nothing ever issues the
connect).  Accept 3 as well.

Also note that the demo's vm/cgame.qvm is API 3 and FTE's CG_Start has no
version check, so only the UI needed relaxing.
---
 plugins/quake3/clq3_ui.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugins/quake3/clq3_ui.c b/plugins/quake3/clq3_ui.c
index 7a1b2c3..8d4e5f6 100644
--- a/plugins/quake3/clq3_ui.c
+++ b/plugins/quake3/clq3_ui.c
@@ -1844,7 +1844,7 @@ void UI_Start (void)
 	if (uivm)
 	{
 		apiversion = vmfuncs->Call(uivm, UI_GETAPIVERSION, 6);
-		if (apiversion != 4 && apiversion != 6)	//make sure we can run the thing
+		if (apiversion != 3 && apiversion != 4 && apiversion != 6)	//make sure we can run the thing (3 = q3 1.11 demo UI)
 		{
 			Con_Printf("User-Interface VM uses incompatible API version (%i)\n", apiversion);
 			vmfuncs->Destroy(uivm);
-- 
